{"author":{"id":"2de4467f26c42fb223f4d3ddd5611e7c0513d3daae4c1dc315de039036bc997d"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1778985378,"nonce":"V8tHru1O1m67dP0ac63mWwN/N0k=","title":"Fix margin-note paragraph hydration regression","message":"## Problem\\nAfter fixing nested directive conversion, targeted margin notes inside note scopes now render as components, but container-style margin notes can carry paragraph block children into an inline note anchor. On /blog/hashing-python-functions, React reports that \u003cp\u003e cannot be a descendant of \u003cp\u003e: the outer MDX paragraph contains a note anchor/span, and the nested MarginNote renders its content as a child \u003cp\u003e.\\n\\n## Context\\nThe prior fix for issue 5e0160e changed directive conversion from SKIP-based visitor replacement to recursive conversion, which exposed this separate invalid-HTML problem. The intended behavior is still correct: nested margin notes should be real MarginNote components, but inline-anchored margin notes must not introduce block paragraph descendants inside an existing paragraph.\\n\\n## Potential Solutions\\n- When converting margin-note container directives, unwrap a single paragraph child into phrasing children so inline note anchors do not contain nested \u003cp\u003e elements.\\n- Add a regression smoke test that compiles a paragraph containing a note-scope margin note and checks that no paragraph is nested inside another paragraph in the emitted structure or rendered HTML.\\n- Keep the broader note-system redesign tracked separately in b0115b4.","files":null}]}